{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:38.898811+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Hi, thanks for the question!\n\nUp front, we should recognize that raising an error is a side-effect, and the explicit API contract of `pure_callback` is that the function passed to it should have pure semantics (i.e. no side-effects). Since your example violates this API contract, the expected behavior here is undefined, and we could probably close this issue as \"working as intended\".\n\nThat said, I understand that equinox uses (mis-uses?) `pure_callback` in order to raise value-dependent errors at runtime. This is not something we on the JAX team would recommend (and in fact we've explicitly said this in past discussions with the Equinox team about `error_if`).\n\nI believe what's happening here is that the compiler notices that the callback function always returns None, and since the API contract means the compiler can assume the callback is pure, then there's no reason to actually execute the callback since we know its return value before executing it (note that `scan` will implicitly JIT-compile the `step` function). You can see this by printing the uncompiled HLO and the compiled HLO, and recognizing that the `callback` has been elided in the first example:\n```python\nprint(\"callback\" in jax.jit(f).lower(arr).as_text())  # True\nprint(\"callback\" in jax.jit(f).lower(arr).compile().as_text())  # False\n\nprint(\"callback\" in jax.jit(f).lower(arr2).as_text())  # True\nprint(\"callback\" in jax.jit(f).lower(arr2).compile().as_text())  # True\n```\nThis is a valid optimization for the compiler to make, because the user has specified that the callback function is pure.\n\nI don't have any fix to suggest, beyond the one I've recommended in the past, i.e. that equinox should stop misusing `pure_callback` in this way. You might be able to find a workaround by injecting some data dependence into the callback so that the compiler won't elide it (e.g. something like returning `0` and adding it to the value you're checking), but fundamentally this will continue to be a brittle and unsupported use of JAX APIs.","created_at":"2025-11-06T19:11:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147#issuecomment-3498997066","id":3498997066,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc7QjnVK","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":2,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":2,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3498997066/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-11-06T19:23:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3498997066","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Thank you for the thorough explanation! That does make a lot of sense to me. \n\nWhat I do find interesting is that whether or not the compiler makes this optimisation seems to have something to do with the size of the input array. Is that expected? Our most frequent use case is reporting on errata such as failed linear solves coming from another library, and for these use cases we have not yet seen it break. \n\nThanks for suggesting the workaround! I agree that that sounds a bit brittle, perhaps we'll still find another way. \n\nThanks again!","created_at":"2025-11-06T20:13:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147#issuecomment-3499220188","id":3499220188,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc7Qkdzc","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499220188/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-11-06T20:13:09Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499220188","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38662446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/johannahaffner","id":38662446,"login":"johannahaffner","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NjYyNDQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"I'm not certain why the compiler elides the callback in one case but not the other: the set of heuristics the compiler uses is large and always growing!\n\nYou could probably focus on just the jit-compiled `step` function to narrow-down the difference.","created_at":"2025-11-06T20:18:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147#issuecomment-3499235598","id":3499235598,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc7QkhkO","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":1,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499235598/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-11-06T20:18:05Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499235598","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Also - you might want to check out [`jax.experimental.io_callback`](https://docs.jax.dev/en/latest/_autosummary/jax.experimental.io_callback.html): this is a callback where the function explicitly has side-effects, and so the compiler shouldn't elide it.\n\nThere are still problems with raising an error at runtime, particularly on accelerators like TPU that don't support runtime aborts. Using this for `error_if` might fix some issues compared to `pure_callback`, but overall the behavior is still not well-defined.","created_at":"2025-11-06T20:20:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147#issuecomment-3499244614","id":3499244614,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc7QkjxG","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499244614/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-11-06T20:21:21Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499244614","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Ah that is interesting! I'll check out `io_callback`, perhaps that can future proof our runtime errata. We do handle TPUs as a special case already, perhaps we could just continue doing that. \n\nThank you for the support!","created_at":"2025-11-06T20:53:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147#issuecomment-3499352120","id":3499352120,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc7Qk-A4","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499352120/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-11-06T20:53:25Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3499352120","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38662446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/johannahaffner","id":38662446,"login":"johannahaffner","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NjYyNDQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannahaffner","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### Description\n\nThe following code raises a runtime error when scanning over a two-dimensional array, unless the two-dimensional array only has a single row. \nWhen I add a `debug.print` to examine `pred`, I do get the expected values, but the error still only triggers for the single-row array.\n\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jaxtyping import Array, Float\n\n\ndef error_if(x, pred, msg):\n    def raises(args):\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{msg}\\n\\n\\n\")\n\n    def handle_error():  # pyright: ignore\n        out = jax.pure_callback(raises, struct, None)\n        return out\n\n    struct = jax.eval_shape(lambda: x)\n    return jax.lax.cond(pred, handle_error, lambda: x)\n\n\ndef f(arr: Float[Array, \"n d\"]):\n    def access(state: int):\n        pred = state >= arr.shape[0]\n        state = error_if(state, pred, \"State exceeds array bounds.\")\n        return arr[state]\n\n    def step(carry, i):\n        state = carry\n        value = access(state)\n        state += 1\n        return state, value\n\n    init_state = 0\n    final_state, values = jax.lax.scan(step, init_state, length=3)\n    return values\n\n\narr = jnp.array([[7.0, 13.0]])\nprint(f(arr), arr)\nprint(\"\\n\\n\\n\")\n\narr2 = jnp.array([[7.0, 13.0], [1.0, 2.0]])\nprint(f(arr2), arr2)\n```\n\nCross-referencing https://github.com/patrick-kidger/equinox/issues/1142. \n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```\njax:    0.7.2\njaxlib: 0.7.2\nnumpy:  2.3.3\npython: 3.13.3 (main, Apr  8 2025, 13:54:08) [Clang 16.0.0 (clang-1600.0.26.6)]\ndevice info: cpu-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Darwin', node='REDACTED', release='24.5.0', version='Darwin Kernel Version 24.5.0: Tue Apr 22 19:54:26 PDT 2025; root:xnu-11417.121.6~2/RELEASE_ARM64_T8112', machine='arm64')\n```","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147/comments","created_at":"2025-11-06T17:47:54Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/33147","id":3596869837,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived